<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ndyuka</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Aukan, Ndyuka people</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ndyuka are a maroon people of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suriname">Suriname</a> and French Guiana, descended from enslaved Africans who escaped from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> plantations into the rainforest in the 18th century. After years of conflict the colonial government made a peace treaty with them in 1760, recognising their freedom. They live mainly along the Tapanahony and Marowijne rivers under their own paramount chief, the gaanman.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ndyuka.jpg" alt="Ndyuka" width="320" height="234" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tropenmuseum_Royal_Tropical_Institute_Objectnumber_10031753_Groepsportret_van_Aukaner_Marrons_in.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
